  "body": "I am trying to build a loading indicator for a responsive image (using `img` element with `srcset` and `sizes`), however it seems there is no reliable way to detect when an image *starts* loading.\r\n\r\nFor responsive images, `currentSrc` can change at any time, for example:\r\n\r\n- on resize\r\n- when `sizes` is changed\r\n\r\nThis marks the beginning of a new image request, via a change to `currentSrc`.\r\n\r\nI am looking for a way to detect when `currentSrc` changes. I can use the `load` event to detect when the `currentSrc` has changed and the request has completed, however I want to detect when the request starts.\r\n\r\nPerhaps we need an event for when `currentSrc` changes?\r\n\r\nPlease let me know if there is a better place to post and discuss this suggestion.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nOliver",
